  "body": "PR #4065 adds the Sodick LN2W wire post (`sodick-ln2w.cps`). The review of head `b12db2f06` found that a tapered cut on that post is not safe yet. Thus the post refuses each tapered cut by name. This issue holds the work that is necessary to post a taper again.\n\nWhat is necessary before the post writes `TP` / `TN`, `G51` / `G52` `A` and `G50`:\n\n1. **The height of the work above the worktable, for each setup.** `TP` and `TN` are heights above the worktable. A value in the machine file is the same for each setup. A 20 mm part on a 5 mm fixture then posts `TP20.` and `TN0.`, but its planes are 25 mm and 5 mm above the table. Add a setup value (a command with its MCP tool), send it in the stream, and refuse a taper when the active setup does not state it.\n2. **The corner motion of the LN2W control under `G51` / `G52`.** No source confirms that the control cuts a mitre corner. A control that rounds the lower corner cuts a different surface from the surface that CamCraft checked. The owner of the AQ600L can confirm it with an air cut. Then state the confirmed rule in `sodick-aq600l.mch`.\n3. **The lean side.** The app signs the stream angle by `edm.taper_angle.positive`. The post must read that rule (mirror it into `machine.edm`) and map the side to `G51` (left) or `G52` (right). Add a case for `top_right`.\n4. **The angle precision.** A nonzero angle below 0.0005 degree rounds to `A0.`. Refuse it, or use a precision that the control is confirmed to read.\n\nThe removed taper code and its goldens are in the history of PR #4065 (head `b12db2f06`): `taperWord`, `taperHeights`, `edm.table_to_part_bottom` and `PARAM WireBottom`.\n\nRefs #4045, #2130, #4065.\n",
